dfB = number of groups - 1
dfW = total number of plants - number of groups

4. Calculate the mean square between groups (MSB) and the mean square within groups (MSW).

MSB = SSB / dfB
MSW = SSW / dfW

5. Calculate the F statistic.

F = MSB / MSW

6. Determine the critical F value using an F-distribution table with dfB and dfW degrees of freedom at a chosen significance level (usually 0.05).

7. Compare the calculated F statistic with the critical F value.

